From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qwen3.8: GDN RecoverSSM - speculative verification without
 state blocks

VLLM_QWEN38_GDN_RECOVER (default 0 = unchanged; align mode). MTP verification
reads the committed state of the running block and records, per request slot
outside the KV pool, the exact operands of each token's state update (decay,
normalised key, correction). After sampling, every PP rank commits on its own
layers in postprocess_state (the non-last rank's deferred postprocess carries
the same accepted counts): the accepted prefix is replayed with the verifying
kernel's update operations (bit-identical state), the boundary state is
written when a 1632-token block boundary is crossed, GDN and PLE conv windows
are compacted and num_accepted reset, so the align pre/postprocess and the
generated-history checkpoints see normalised states. GDN and PLE reserve no
speculative state blocks: with MTP5 a request holds 6 instead of 21 blocks
(c32: KV 27 % instead of 94.5 %, no preemption).

Verification uses a native copy of the fused CUDA MTP decode kernel
(models/qwen3.8-flash-next-nvfp4/native/gdn_mtp_record, built into the image,
same flags as _C) with a recording mode; without the library it falls back to
the Triton recording kernel. Greedy outputs are bit-identical to the baseline
(native path vs the fused CUDA kernel; Triton path vs the Triton kernel).
Adapted from the Kimi KDA RecoverSSM design (vLLM PR #58863 for Qwen GDN),
extended to pipeline parallelism.
